@startuml
title Sequence Diagram(Resident Pickup Handover)
autonumber

actor "Resident" as Resident
actor "Staff" as Staff
participant "Web Client" as Web
participant "PickupController" as PKC
participant "PickupService" as PKS
participant "AuditService" as AS
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

Resident -> Staff : Shows the pickup code
Staff -> Web : Enter the code
Web -> PKC : POST /pickup/verify
activate PKC
PKC -> PKS : verify(code)
activate PKS
PKS -> DB : select PickupCode by code
DB --> PKS : code row
PKS -> PKS : reject unless the code is active and unexpired
PKS --> PKC : parcel and storage location
deactivate PKS
PKC --> Web : 200 OK
deactivate PKC

Web --> Staff : Shows the parcel and where it is
Staff -> Web : Confirm the handover
Web -> PKC : POST /pickup/confirm
activate PKC
PKC -> PKS : confirm(pickupCodeId)
activate PKS
PKS -> DB : begin transaction
PKS -> DB : lock the PickupCode row
PKS -> DB : PickupCode status to used
PKS -> DB : Parcel status to picked_up
PKS -> DB : Location status to available
PKS -> DB : insert Handover with result collected
PKS -> AS : record HANDOVER_CONFIRMED
PKS -> DB : commit
PKS --> PKC : HandoverSummary
deactivate PKS
PKC --> Web : 201 Created
deactivate PKC

Web --> Staff : Handover recorded
Staff --> Resident : Gives the parcel

note over PKS
  Confirming the same code twice returns the
  original handover instead of creating a
  second one. Handover is idempotent by
  pickupCodeId, and the code is single use.
end note

note over DB
  One transaction covers the code, the parcel,
  the location and the handover row so that a
  failure cannot leave a parcel marked as
  collected while its location is still occupied.
end note
@enduml